{"page": 502, "row_type": "row", "section": "WHITE BEAR'S RESERVE, NO. 70.", "label": "60", "values": ["Pa-pa-mas", "6", "...", "6", "1", "...", "...", "...", "20", "...", "10", "4", "...", "...", "...", "This is an approximate estimate, as the grain was not threshed, a stack containing about 50 bushels has been burned. When the Reserve was last visited the Indians were almost all away and their cellars could not be seen. Besides the failure in crops common this year to this section of the country, a large proportion of their standing grain was ruined by their cattle. Many of their potatoes"], "confidence": "medium"}
